diff --git a/docs/bots.md b/docs/bots.md
index 210c6b6..40fe619 100644
--- a/docs/bots.md
+++ b/docs/bots.md
@@ -131,3 +131,25 @@ Implementation note: membership grants retain bulk inserts for people, but bots
 use callback-enabled, idempotent creation backed by the unique room/user index.
 Keep future bot membership creation paths callback-enabled so they also send
 joined events. Do not perform HTTP requests from membership callbacks.
+
+## Bots per member
+
+Administrators configure **Bots per member** in account settings. The integer
+setting lives in the existing account JSON settings and defaults to 5, including
+for accounts saved before this setting existed. Zero disables new bots for
+members; administrators remain unlimited. Negative and blank limits are rejected.
+
+`User#can_create_bot?` counts the creator's active bots, matching the bot management
+page. Deleting a bot deactivates it and frees a slot. The creation-only validation
+in `User::Bot` also protects direct POSTs and model creation outside the management
+controller. Lowering the limit does not deactivate or prevent editing existing
+bots. Creation resumes once the member is below the limit again.
+
+The quota check runs inside Active Record's save transaction. The app's SQLite
+configuration uses immediate transactions, serializing writers across the count
+and insert. If the database adapter or transaction mode changes, preserve that
+serialization (for example, with a creator row lock) to prevent concurrent bot
+creation from exceeding the quota.
+
+Regression coverage is in `test/models/user/bot_test.rb`, the account and bot
+controller tests, and `test/system/bots_test.rb`.
diff --git a/test/controllers/accounts_controller_test.rb b/test/controllers/accounts_controller_test.rb
index 8292c6f..074c39a 100644
--- a/test/controllers/accounts_controller_test.rb
+++ b/test/controllers/accounts_controller_test.rb
@@ -58,4 +58,30 @@ class AccountsControllerTest < ActionDispatch::IntegrationTest
     put account_url, params: { account: { name: "Different" } }
     assert_response :forbidden
   end
+
+  test "administrators can configure bots per member" do
+    get edit_account_url
+    assert_select 'label[for="account_settings_bots_per_member"]', text: "Bots per member"
+    assert_select 'input[type="number"][name="account[settings][bots_per_member]"][value="5"]'
+
+    put account_url, params: { account: { settings: { bots_per_member: "2" } } }
+    assert_redirected_to edit_account_url
+    assert_equal 2, accounts(:signal).reload.settings.bots_per_member
+  end
+
+  test "members cannot see or change the bot limit" do
+    sign_in :kevin
+    get edit_account_url
+    assert_select 'input[name="account[settings][bots_per_member]"]', count: 0
+    put account_url, params: { account: { settings: { bots_per_member: "100" } } }
+    assert_response :forbidden
+    assert_equal 5, accounts(:signal).reload.settings.bots_per_member
+  end
+
+  test "invalid bot limits render errors without changing the account" do
+    put account_url, params: { account: { settings: { bots_per_member: "-1" } } }
+    assert_response :unprocessable_entity
+    assert_select '[role="alert"]', text: /Bots per member/
+    assert_equal 5, accounts(:signal).reload.settings.bots_per_member
+  end
 end
